# Ooda Router — Dispatch Pattern
File: ooda/docs/dispatch.oot

The ooda binary is a thin argv router in `ooda/main.oo`. Language verbs
spawn `cli`. Package drivers spawn `opm`, `lsp`, `mcp`, or `tui`.
Deprecated verbs print a moved error and exit 2. `help` and `version`
stay in-process. There is no in-process `run_oodac_build` in this tree.

## The mental model

```
user types:  ooda build src/main.oo
                │
                ▼
        ooda/main.oo argv router
                │
                ▼
        spawn("cli", ["build", "src/main.oo"])
                │
                ▼
        cli binary runs run_oodac_build
                │
                ▼
        ooda exits with the same code
```

`ooda qa` is the same path: the router forwards to `cli qa`, and cli
builds `qa/suite.oo`. The router does not run probes itself.

The router is the only place that decides which binary runs. Spawned
handlers never see `argv[0]` as a router name; they receive the
subcommand rest (language verbs prepend the verb for cli).

## The dispatch shape

```oo
pub fn main(...args: List[String]) -> Result[Int, String] {
    if list_len(args) < 1 {
        return spawn(fs_r, env, sys, "tui", list_new());
    }
    let sub: String = list_get(args, 0);
    let rest: List[String] = list_slice(args, 1, list_len(args));

    if sub == "opm" { return spawn(fs_r, env, sys, "opm", rest); }
    if sub == "lsp" { return spawn(fs_r, env, sys, "lsp", rest); }
    if sub == "mcp" { return spawn(fs_r, env, sys, "mcp", rest); }
    if sub == "tui" { return spawn(fs_r, env, sys, "tui", rest); }

    if sub == "build" { return forward_to_cli(fs_r, env, sys, "build", rest); }
    if sub == "qa"    { return forward_to_cli(fs_r, env, sys, "qa", rest); }

    if sub == "digest" {
        println("ooda: digest moved to `bb digest <file>`.");
        process_exit(2);
        return Err("ooda: digest moved");
    }

    if sub == "help" { router_help(); return Ok(0); }
    router_help();
    process_exit(2);
    return Err("ooda: unknown subcommand: " + sub);
}
```

`forward_to_cli` prepends `sub` and calls `spawn(..., "cli", margs)`.
The cascade is `if`, not `match`, so upgrade can alias update and
mcp-merge can prepend its own verb before spawn.

## The lifecycle: parse, route, spawn, report

### 1. Parse

`main.oo` reads `argv[0]` as the subcommand and slices `argv[1..]` as
the tail. Empty argv opens ooda-tui.

### 2. Route

Language verbs go to cli. Driver verbs go to that package binary.
Deprecated verbs (eval, repl, bench, gen, health, digest, sandbox,
swarm) print a moved line and exit 2. Unknown names print help and
exit 2.

### 3. Spawn

`build/spawn.oo` resolves `$OODACODEX/bin/<name>` (or `OODA_CODEX`,
`~/.openooda/bin`, or dirname of `OODA_COMPILER`). Names with `/` or
`..` fail closed. There is no `$PATH` lookup. Stdio is inherited.

### 4. Report

Spawned handlers return the child exit code. In-process help and
version return `Ok(0)`. Moved and unknown paths call `process_exit(2)`.

## Naming

| Name | Where | Role |
|------|-------|------|
| `forward_to_cli` | `main.oo` | spawn cli with `[sub, ...rest]` |
| `spawn` | `build/spawn.oo` | resolve and exec an external binary |
| `router_help` | `main.oo` | print the router table |
| `run_oodac_build` | `cli/build/host_build.oo` | not called from ooda/main.oo |

## Why subprocess for cli, opm, lsp, mcp, tui?

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Why subprocess? | Version decoupling. Each driver has its own VERSION. |
| Why stdio-inherited? | Editors connect stdio to ooda; lsp/mcp need that stdio. |
| Why is ooda the meta-router? | One command, many packages. |
| Why no library link? | Linking creates a hard version dep. |

## What stays in-process

- `help`, `--help`, `-h`
- `version`, `--version`, `-v`
- Moved-error printers (exit 2)

These do not have their own packages. The ooda binary is the only home.

## What gets spawned

Language CLI (forwarded as `cli <sub>`):

- build, run, test, fmt, install, update, upgrade, init, qa, context, fix, token

External drivers:

- `opm`, `lsp`, `mcp`, `tui`
- `mcp-merge` spawns `mcp` with a leading `mcp-merge` verb

`run_oodac_build` lives in cli. `bb digest` / `bb bench` / `bb health`
live in bb. `opm gen` lives in opm. eval/repl and sandbox/swarm run
paths live in ooda-tui.

## Failure paths

| Failure | Source | Exit code | Output |
|---------|--------|-----------|--------|
| empty argv | `main.oo` | child | opens ooda-tui |
| unknown subcommand | `main.oo` | 2 | help text + `Err("ooda: unknown subcommand: <name>")` |
| moved verb | `main.oo` | 2 | `ooda: <verb> moved ...` |
| missing spawn binary | `build/spawn.oo` | 1 | `ERR spawn <msg>` |
| subprocess failure | spawn | child | whatever the child printed |
